<title>UK: Licht sees EU 1996/97 sugar output at 17.81 mln t.</title>
<headline>Licht sees EU 1996/97 sugar output at 17.81 mln t.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar production in the European Union (EU) should rise to 17.81 million tonnes raw value in 1996/97, up from 17.00 million in 1995/96, statistician F.O. Licht said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In its second estimate of world 1996/97 sugar production, Licht said the expected increase in the EU could be attributed to late beet development due to favourable autumn weather conditions.</p>
<p>&quot;The autumn weather was very favourable to beet sugar production in Europe and output in the EU is now put at 17.8 million tonnes, raw value, up by 806,000 tonnes after 476,000 tonnes the previous season.&quot;</p>
<p>Licht's first estimate of world sugar outputs, released in October, showed the EU with a figure of 16.86 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
